{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1473","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1473","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1473\",\"parent_revision\":\"6e83df839a79e8e88a194d1013dad59bb7142bd592325c6469fd467f3de971c6\",\"root_revision\":\"6e83df839a79e8e88a194d1013dad59bb7142bd592325c6469fd467f3de971c6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter the P1422 rendering abstraction, github_sync.py still independently defines SECTION_HEADING at line 44 with the same values as rendering.SECTION_HEADING (lines 34\u201338). The constant is still exported in github_sync.__all__ (line 25) and used internally at lines 51 (_HEADING_TO_KEY), 54 (_KNOWN_SECTION_KEYS), and 193 (render_issue_body loop).\\n\\nThis creates a dual-definition risk: a future edit to rendering.SECTION_HEADING that adds or renames a key will not propagate to github_sync._HEADING_TO_KEY or _KNOWN_SECTION_KEYS, causing silent parsing divergence.\\n\\nThe correct fix is:\\n1. Replace the local definition in github_sync.py (lines 44\u201348) with: from .rendering import SECTION_HEADING\\n2. Remove SECTION_HEADING from github_sync.__all__ \u2014 callers should import from rendering.\\n3. Verify _HEADING_TO_KEY and _KNOWN_SECTION_KEYS still derive correctly (they will, since they reference SECTION_HEADING by name).\\n\\nNo behavioural change \u2014 both dicts contain identical values today.\\n\\nFiles: plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py (lines 25, 44\u201354, 193), plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/rendering.py (unchanged \u2014 canonical source).\\n\\nEffort: XS. Plan: plan/P1422-github-sync-section-heading-dedup-followup-1.yaml\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Exact lines confirmed in item description | AVAILABLE | github_sync.py lines 25, 44-54, 193; rendering.py lines 34-38 |\\n| 2 | `rendering.SECTION_HEADING` is the canonical source | AVAILABLE | Item description |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 XS effort, fully specified.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Refactor. XS effort. Zero behavioral change. Eliminates dual-definition drift risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `github_sync.py` line 44 local definition of `SECTION_HEADING` replaced with: `from .rendering import SECTION_HEADING`\\n- `SECTION_HEADING` removed from `github_sync.__all__` (line 25)\\n- `_HEADING_TO_KEY` and `_KNOWN_SECTION_KEYS` at lines 51-54 still derive correctly (they reference `SECTION_HEADING` by name, so no change needed)\\n- `render_issue_body` loop at line 193 unaffected\\n- `ruff check` and `ty check` pass\\n- Zero behavioral change \u2014 both dicts contain identical values\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py` \u2014 lines 25, 44-54 (replace definition with import, remove from __all__)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a backlog_core maintainer, I need `github_sync.py` to import `SECTION_HEADING` from `rendering.py` instead of redefining it identically so that future edits to the canonical definition in rendering.py propagate automatically without silent divergence.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **remove duplicate section_heading from github_sync \u2014 replace with import from rendering** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | plan/P1422-github-sync-section-heading-dedup-followup-1.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-04T20:04:18Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review finding during P1422 QG T1 (quality gate code-reviewer agent)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dff4625f57e77b946671dfa51de7ab9346026632a300b06a9d8108bf29f8f84f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS917Q\"}"}